id: pm-cyrfjq
title: "Mode-paired envelopes zero-fill the inactive collection instead of omitting it, so parsing the obvious key returns an empty array that is indistinguishable from a real empty result"
description: "pm history --json reports count:7 with history:[] and compact_history populated; --full inverts it. pm-p3x4 records the identical shape on pm activity. Two independent commands sharing the defect means the envelope contract lacks a rule for mode-inactive collection keys, and [] is the one option that cannot be told apart from a legitimate empty result. Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched decoy-key/empty-array/envelope/output-contract items across all statuses; pm-p3x4 is the pm activity instance, pm-srns owns the uniform envelope spec, pm-psy1 owns stable field-name guarantees. No item states the cross-command rule."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[6]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:contracts",output-contract,scripting,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-26T05:43:39.360Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T06:08:41.764Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The output contract states that a row collection belonging to an inactive output mode is omitted rather than zero-filled, in both JSON and TOON; a contract-driven test enumerates every command declaring mutually exclusive output modes and asserts only the active collection key is present, so new commands inherit the assertion by declaration; pm history and pm activity are fixed as the first subjects and pm-p3x4 closes against this rule with its reproduction retained as the negative-control fixture; the envelope carries an explicit mode discriminator wherever the active mode is not otherwise inferable; the behaviour change from [] to absent is documented as a compatibility note in release output rather than shipped silently; the sweep covers at minimum history, activity, graph --summary, context depth tiers, health brief/summary/full, and validate detail rows"
goal: project management = context management
objective: An envelope never emits a key whose emptiness lies about which mode produced it
value: Agents and scripts stop silently reading zero rows from a command that reported a nonzero count; the failure becomes loud at the point of the mistake
why_now: "Found on pm history while probing the history and restore surface, which is the flagship immutability story; the same shape was already filed once for pm activity, so the generator is still live"
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: high
